  "issue_title": "feat(fitness): implement the HERO dense reward (improvement #3, Stage A)",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\nThe `hero_dense` flag in `FitnessConfig` was **reserved but did nothing** (`fitness.py`: *\"Reserved flag for a future per-turn 'hero' dense reward. Currently unused\"*). This implements the documented **Stage-A recipe** from `docs/IMPROVEMENTS.md` #3:\n\n> *a HERO dense quality proxy in [0,1] (self-consistency vote fraction across turns\u2026), min-max normalized **within** the correct and incorrect buckets so a correct answer always outranks a wrong one.*\n\nStage B (variance reweighting) already shipped; this is the un-built other half. **TRAINING fitness only; default-off**, so behavior is unchanged unless enabled.\n\n## What it does\n- **`hero_quality(traj) \u2192 [0,1]`** \u2014 self-consistency: of the trajectory's answer-bearing turns (`reward.has_answer`), the fraction whose answer *agrees* with the committed final answer (`reward.committed_answer`). Agreement reuses the eval scorer's own extractors (choice letter / math value / code), so \"agrees\" means exactly what \"correct\" means. Pure, torch-free.\n- **`hero_bucket_bonus(qualities, corrects, cfg)`** \u2014 min-max normalizes the quality **within** the correct and incorrect buckets, scaled by `cfg.hero_bonus` (default `0.05`, the same scale as `format_bonus`/`turn_penalty`). A degenerate bucket (one value / one member) gets a neutral `0.5` so it can't spuriously reorder candidates.\n- **`evaluate_candidate`** adds the bonus at the batch level (bucket normalization needs the whole minibatch); failed trajectories are excluded.\n- `FitnessConfig` gains `hero_bonus`; `configs/trinity.yaml` documents both knobs.\n\n## Invariants (why it's safe)\n- **Correct always outranks wrong** \u2014 the bonus is added on top of the binary correctness anchor with magnitude `\u2264 hero_bonus`, so worst-correct > best-wrong. Verified **exhaustively** in tests (sweep over turns \u00d7 format \u00d7 hero for both buckets).\n- **Default-off = no-op** \u2014 `hero_dense=False` (the default) skips the block entirely; the current mean-binary fitness is reproduced exactly.\n- **Eval path untouched** \u2014 `reward.score` / `trinity.eval` stay pure binary; this shapes CMA-ES *training* fitness only.\n\n## Testing\n`tests/test_hero_dense.py` (offline, numpy-only, **no torch**): self-consistency across math/MCQ/code, bucket min-max, degenerate-bucket neutrality, `[0, hero_bonus]` bounds, the correct-always-outranks-wrong invariant, and config wiring. **Full suite green (450 passed); ruff + `mypy src/ scripts/repo_governance/` clean.**\n\nScope note: this lands the Stage-A *implementation* behind the existing default-off flag, exactly per the recipe. The doc's success criterion is an empirical A/B (*lower cross-seed variance, no worse mean*) on held-out seeds \u2014 that's a GPU training run to be done by whoever owns the pool; this PR makes that A/B possible by providing the code, unit-tested and reversible.",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T04:10:20.000Z",
